    "research": {
      "notes": "## 1. Guidance and results\n\n- No new guidance or pre-announcement found in the window. The last guidance was given with FQ4 results on 2026-07-29.\n- That guidance included FQ1 revenue of $89.85–90.95B, FY27 capex of about $175B, and double-digit revenue and operating-income growth for FY27. \nFull-year operating margin is expected to decline slightly.\n — 2026-07-29 — https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/microsoft-q4-earnings-call-highlights-000355148.html\n- Azure growth was guided to about 45% in constant currency for FQ1. — 2026-07-29 — https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/microsoft-q4-earnings-call-highlights-000355148.html\n- FQ4 results beat expectations. \nAdjusted EPS was $4.74 on revenue of $90.01B, against expectations of $4.24 and $87.61B.\n — 2026-07-29 — https://www.investing.com/news/earnings/microsoft-beats-on-profit-and-revenue-shares-rise-after-hours-4821565\n- The 8-K says \nresults included a $3.2B gain from the Anthropic investment.\n — 2026-07-29 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/Archives/edgar/data/0000789019/000119312526323632/msft-ex99_1.htm\n- FQ1 results are expected around 2026-10-28, which is not confirmed. \nConsensus is about $90.7B revenue and $4.72 EPS.\n — 2026-10-08 — https://www.cmelitegroup.co.tt/knowledge-hub/microsoft-earnings-date-fiscal-q1-2027-report-time-estimates-and-expected-move/\n\n## 2. Analyst actions\n\n- Citizens maintained Market Outperform at $550. — 2026-09-15 — https://www.benzinga.com/quote/MSFT/price-targets\n- Cantor Fitzgerald raised its target from $522 to $608 (Overweight). — 2026-09-21 — https://www.benzinga.com/quote/MSFT/price-targets\n- Oppenheimer raised its target from $515 to $570 (Outperform). — 2026-09-22 — https://www.benzinga.com/quote/MSFT/price-targets\n- Stifel upgraded from Hold to Buy and raised its target from $530 to $575. Benzinga dates this 2026-09-23 (https://www.benzinga.com/quote/MSFT/price-targets). MarketBeat dates it 2026-09-22 (https://www.marketbeat.com/instant-alerts/analyst-microsoft-nasdaq-msft-rating-lowered-to-hold-at-phillip-securities-2026-10-14/).\n- Piper Sandler raised its target from $550 to $610 (Overweight). — 2026-09-30 — https://www.benzinga.com/quote/MSFT/price-targets\n- Wells Fargo raised its target from $700 to $725 (Overweight). — 2026-10-01 — https://www.benzinga.com/quote/MSFT/price-targets\n- Melius Research upgraded to Buy from Hold with a $665 target. — 2026-10-05 — https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/microsoft-upgraded-hubspot-initiated-wall-134952467.html\n- Scotiabank raised its target from $510 to $615. — 2026-10-05 — https://www.tipranks.com/stocks/msft/forecast\n- Yorkville Ives initiated coverage with a Buy and a $615 target. TipRanks dates it 2026-10-06 (https://www.tipranks.com/stocks/msft/forecast). Investing.com dates it 2026-10-07 (https://www.investing.com/equities/microsoft-corp-consensus-estimates).\n- Evercore ISI has conflicting entries. One source shows a target raise from $528 to $635 on 2026-10-07 (https://tickernerd.com/stock/msft-forecast/). TipRanks shows the Buy rating reiterated with an unchanged $600 target (https://www.tipranks.com/stocks/msft/forecast).\n- Phillip Securities downgraded from Moderate Buy to Hold. — 2026-10-12 — https://www.marketbeat.com/instant-alerts/analyst-microsoft-nasdaq-msft-rating-lowered-to-hold-at-phillip-securities-2026-10-14/\n- Phillip's target is $515. — 2026-10-12 — https://www.investing.com/equities/microsoft-corp-consensus-estimates\n- Deutsche Bank maintained Hold and raised its target from $550 to $600. — 2026-10-12 — https://www.investing.com/equities/microsoft-corp-consensus-estimates\n- Barclays raised its target from $512 to $600 (Overweight). Investing.com dates this 2026-10-12 (https://www.investing.com/equities/microsoft-corp-consensus-estimates). GuruFocus dates it 2026-10-13 (https://www.gurufocus.com/news/9121386/msft-maintained-by-barclays-price-target-raised-to-600).\n- MarketBeat's average target is $581.80. \nIt counts 41 Buy, five Hold and two Sell ratings.\n — 2026-10-14 — https://www.marketbeat.com/instant-alerts/analyst-microsoft-nasdaq-msft-rating-lowered-to-hold-at-phillip-securities-2026-10-14/\n- That MarketBeat page also lists a Citigroup move from \"market outperform\" to \"buy\" on 2026-10-05. \"Market outperform\" is a Citizens rating label, so the attribution may be wrong. Treat it as unverified.\n\n## 3. Litigation and regulation\n\n- Italy's antitrust authority opened an EU-backed probe into Microsoft-owned game makers, including Activision Blizzard, over virtual currencies. — 2026-10-08 — https://www.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/italy-launches-eubacked-probe-into-microsoftowned-gaming-companies-4938621\n- The FTC's broad cloud, licensing, security and AI/Copilot probe is reportedly still active. \nIt began as a civil investigative demand in November 2024.\n The tech-insider.org article says the inquiry widened and is a secondary source. — date unknown — https://tech-insider.org/microsoft-antitrust-probe-cloud-ai-2026/\n- A headline on cloudcomputing-news.net says AWS and Azure face EU gatekeeper rules over cloud lock-in. I found no detail. — 2026-10-05 — https://www.cloudcomputing-news.net/news/anthropic-ai-infrastructure-518-billion/\n- No fines, court rulings or export-control actions found in the window.\n\n## 4. Customer concentration\n\n- OpenAI is the largest related-party customer. \nFY2026 revenue from OpenAI was $24.1B, with $6.0B of receivables at 2026-06-30.\n — 2026-06-30 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0000789019/000119312526323660/msft-20260630.htm\n- The OpenAI contract was amended earlier: \nMicrosoft remains primary cloud partner, OpenAI can use any cloud, and Microsoft's IP license is non-exclusive.\n — 2026-04-27 — https://openai.com/index/next-phase-of-microsoft-partnership/\n-",
